A||||7||mrfixit58||How'd Water Get in There?||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-18-2001||02:38 PM||||My trunk, that is. We've had a couple of blinding rain storms lately and I've noticed that my trunk is getting a fair amount of water inside. It's happening when it's parked. My weather stripping is in good shape and I can't see a trace of water on the lid. I do see some evidence on drips on the driver's side ledge. Has anyone experienced this?<P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-18-2001||03:10 PM||||Yes in my 88GT on the passenger side inside the trunk.  I was told that the leak comes from the wing mounting bolts.  But mine have already been gooped up.  The trunk gasket is new.  I still get water in.<P>I'd like some ideas too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||07-18-2001||05:21 PM||||I forgot to mention... I got no wing... never did.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||07-18-2001||06:24 PM||||Pull back the carpet on the sides of the trunk. <BR>A few inches down from the top is where they commonly rust through. <BR>Hopefully, that's not the case.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||West Coast Fiero||07-18-2001||06:41 PM||||check to see if the "water plugs" are there at the bottom of the trunk, if so make sure they are properly sealed, maybe use some RTV<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJET||07-18-2001||07:39 PM||||I too have this problem on my 86 GT.  Trunk seal is new and I have put RTV around the nuts to the wing.  I noticed that it stopped leaking around the wing bolts but it still leaks on the drivers side.  If I check it after a good rain the carpet is wet on the frontside left of the trunk.  ||||reg||5
Z||000006||fierodave||07-19-2001||07:10 AM||||Had the same problem in a 86 GT  took me two weeks to figure it out.<P>on each side of the trunk there is a plastic Square off part...it's for the gt's only it makes the trunk square in the gt  <P>Mine had a crack in that plastic part on the drivers side and it happened after I replaced a trunk gasket that didn't leak! :~( but looked bad.  <P>I must have cracked it pressing the new gasket into place!   <P>Stand on your head in the trunk and run a water hose next to the open lid where the gasket is next to the black inner sail windows.<BR>and look under it and you will see the leak about 4 inches in...at that plastic part!  <P>I pulled the gasket back out and gooped the square off plastic parts with 3M black super weather stripe adheasive,  put in the gasket again and all is well!<BR>Hope it helps you guys  let me know if it does!<BR>FD<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.theglobe.com/fierodave/gifs/fierosig.gif">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 07-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfixit58||07-19-2001||09:51 AM||||Thanks guys,<P>Since this is a California car, there isn't a speck of rust on it. and the leak happens when it parked so the plug can't be the culprit.<P>Dave, I'll check it out. I replaced my trunk seal as well. <P>Roy<P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||14
